    "answer": "The provided records do not give a direct formal definition of a ration card. However, based on the available information, it is a card issued by State or Union Territory (UT) governments to eligible households (such as Priority Households (PHH) and Antyodaya Anna Yojana (AAY)) under the National Food Security Act (NFSA). It allows beneficiaries to get their entitled subsidised or free foodgrains from Fair Price Shops (FPS), including across the country under the One Nation One Ration Card (ONORC) plan.",
